    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0477" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/>

                <head>No. 284.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 29, 1872</date>.
                        (Received February 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 507.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 505, I have
                    the honor to inclose a copy and translation (A and B) of another article by Mr.
                    Emilio Velaso. published in the Siglo XIX of the 10th instant, upon the subject
                    of the Free Zone,</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d284-a1.xml" xpointer="d284-a1"/>
